ign with federated databases and machine learning", "publisher": "Materials Cloud", "publication_date": "2026-03-12", "subjects": [{"subject": "electronic structure"}, {"subject": "OPTIMADE"}, {"subject": "optical materials"}, {"subject": "refractive index"}, {"subject": "MODNet"}], "contributors": [{"person_or_org": {"type": "personal", "name": "Evans, Matthew L.", "given_name": "Matthew L.", "family_name": "Evans", "identifiers": [{"identifier": "0000-0002-1182-9098", "scheme": "orcid"}]}, "role": {"id": "contactperson", "title": {"de": "Kontaktperson", "en": "Contact person"}}, "affiliations": [{"name": "UCLouvain, Institut de la Matiere Condens\u00e9e et des Nanosciences (IMCN), Chemin des \u00c9toiles 8, Louvain-la-Neuve 1348, Belgium"}, {"name": "Matgenix SRL, 185 Rue Armand Bury, 6534 Goz\u00e9e, Belgium"}]}, {"person_or_org": {"type": "personal", "name": "Rignanese, Gian-Marco", "given_name": "Gian-Marco", "family_name": "Rignanese", "identifiers": [{"identifier": "0000-0002-1422-1205", "scheme": "orcid"}]}, "role": {"id": "contactperson", "title": {"de": "Kontaktperson", "en": "Contact person"}}, "affiliations": [{"name": "UCLouvain, Institut de la Matiere Condens\u00e9e et des Nanosciences (IMCN), Chemin des \u00c9toiles 8, Louvain-la-Neuve 1348, Belgium"}]}], "languages": [{"id": "eng", "title": {"en": "English"}}], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.12545611", "scheme": "doi", "relation_type": {"id": "issupplementto", "title": {"en": "Is supplement to"}}, "resource_type": {"id": "software", "title": {"de": "Software", "en": "Software"}}}, {"identifier": "https://github.com/modl-uclouvain/re2fractive", "scheme": "url", "relation_type": {"id": "issupplementto", "title": {"en": "Is supplement to"}}, "resource_type": {"id": "software", "title": {"de": "Software", "en": "Software"}}}, {"identifier": "10.1039/D4FD00092G", "scheme": "doi", "relation_type": {"id": "issupplementto", "title": {"en": "Is supplement to"}}, "resource_type": {"id": "publication-article", "title": {"en": "Journal article"}}}, {"identifier": "10.48550/arXiv.2405.11393", "scheme": "doi", "relation_type": {"id": "issupplementto", "title": {"en": "Is supplement to"}}, "resource_type": {"id": "publication-preprint", "title": {"en": "Preprint"}}}, {"identifier": "https://chemiscope.materialscloud.io/?load=https%3A%2F%2Farchive.materialscloud.org%2Fapi%2Frecords%2Frr3za-8c528%2Ffiles%2Fdataset_chemiscope.json.gz%2Fcontent%3Ffilename%3Ddataset_chemiscope.json.gz%26materials_cloud_doi%3D10.24435%2Fmaterialscloud%3Akg-ea", "scheme": "url", "relation_type": {"id": "issupplementedby", "title": {"en": "Is supplemented by"}}}], "sizes": ["4831013"], "formats": ["application/gzip", "text/markdown", "application/gzip", "application/gzip", "application/octet-stream"], "rights": [{"id": "cc-by-4.0", "title": {"en": "Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International"}, "description": {"en": "The Creative Commons Attribution license allows re-distribution and re-use of a licensed work on the condition that the creator is appropriately credited."}, "icon": "cc-by-icon", "props": {"url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode", "scheme": "spdx"}}], "description": "Combinatorial and guided screening of materials space with density-functional theory and related approaches has provided a wealth of hypothetical inorganic materials, which are increasingly tabulated in open databases. The OPTIMADE API is a standardised format for representing crystal structures, their measured and computed properties, and the methods for querying and filtering them from remote resources. Currently, the OPTIMADE federation spans over 20 data providers, rendering over 30 million structures accessible in this way, many of which are novel and have only recently been suggested by machine learning-based approaches. In this work, we outline our approach to non-exhaustively screen this dynamic trove of structures for the next-generation of optical materials. By applying MODNet, a neural network-based model for property prediction that has been shown to perform especially well for small materials datasets, within a combined active learning and high-throughput computation framework, we isolate particular structures and chemistries that should be most fruitful for further theoretical calculations and for experimental study as high-refractive-index materials. By making explicit use of automated calculations, federated dataset curation and machine learning, and by releasing these publicly, the workflows presented here can be periodically re-assessed as new databases implement OPTIMADE, and new hypothetical materials are suggested."}, "custom_fields": {"mc_references": [{"ref_resource_type": "software", "ref_citation": "re2fractive GitHub Repository", "ref_link": {"ref_scheme": "doi", "ref_identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.12545611"}, "ref_comment": "Software implementation"}, {"ref_resource_type": "software", "ref_citation": "re2fractive GitHub Repository", "ref_link": {"ref_scheme": "url", "ref_identifier": "https://github.com/modl-uclouvain/re2fractive"}, "ref_comment": "Software implementation"}, {"ref_resource_type": "publication-article", "ref_citation": "V. Trinquet, M. L. Evans, et al., Faraday Discussions (2024)", "ref_link": {"ref_scheme": "doi", "ref_identifier": "10.1039/D4FD00092G"}}, {"ref_resource_type": "publication-preprint", "ref_citation": "V. Trinquet, M. L. Evans, et al., arXiv:2405.11393 (2024)", "ref_link": {"ref_scheme": "doi", "ref_identifier": "10.48550/arXiv.2405.11393"}}]}, "access": {"record": "public", "files": "public", "embargo": {"active": false, "reason": null}, "status": "open"}, "files": {"enabled": true, "order": [], "count": 5, "total_bytes": 4831013, "entries": {"dataset_chemiscope.json.gz": {"id": "575b1b8b-5fc4-4c91-91cd-09df29f3e027", "checksum": "md5:83221bcc8d98cd1cc5a2f1d0f4fba9df", "ext": "gz", "size": 1401448, "mimetype": "application/gzip", "storage_class": "L", "key": "dataset_chemiscope.j